cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  impact-adjoint: exact gradients through impact events across a Julia and JAX
  Tesseract boundary
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Harsh
    family-names: Singh
    alias: singhharsh1708
repository-code: https://github.com/singhharsh1708/impact-adjoint
url: https://impact-adjoint.vercel.app
abstract: >-
  Simulations of contact are easy to write and hard to differentiate: the step
  at which an impact fires is an integer, so automatic differentiation returns
  a gradient that is silently wrong rather than merely inaccurate.
  impact-adjoint computes exact parameter sensitivities across impact events
  using the classical saltation matrix, and serves them from a Julia solver
  through a Tesseract component boundary, so a JAX program obtains the true
  derivative without doing any event handling of its own. The resulting
  gradients design passive structures whose function exists only because of
  impacts.
keywords:
  - differentiable simulation
  - hybrid dynamical systems
  - saltation matrix
  - contact dynamics
  - automatic differentiation
  - inverse design
